{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED. Gerrit 1240 (single-source) + 1241 (guard), stacked on origin/main.\n\nDIFF OF THE TWO COPIES BEFORE UNIFYING (acceptance criterion 1). Re-confirmed in the tree at\nb3bbfecbc4 before touching anything:\n  adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:88 (Cloud)  {\"bug\":\"Bug\",\"story\":\"Story\",\"task\":\"Task\",\"epic\":\"Epic\"}\n  adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:43 (DC)  {\"task\":\"Task\",\"story\":\"Story\",\"bug\":\"Bug\",\"epic\":\"Epic\"}\nSame four keys, same four values, differing ONLY in literal key order — which a dict does not\ncarry semantically. CONTENT-IDENTICAL, so the unification is behaviour-preserving on BOTH\ndeployments and NO divergence decision was required (criterion 2 is satisfied vacuously, and that\nfact is recorded in the value_maps.py comment so the next reader does not have to re-derive it).\n\nCONFIG.PY THIRD-COPY CHECK (criterion 9): config.py:11 is a COMMENT only — no backing literal.\nIndependently corroborated by the new guard, which now walks EVERY dict literal under adapters/\nand finds exactly one.\n\nBINDING: absolute import under the historical private alias, copying the J2 idiom verbatim —\n  from rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira_family import LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA as _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE\nin outbound_fields.py, and the value_maps-direct form of the same in the DC backend. Absolute\ndeliberately: these modules are loaded via spec_from_file_location with no package context in\nseveral tests, where a relative import raises ImportError. NOT tidied to relative (that is\ncc77's requirement, and it applies there because cc77 imports a TYPE used in annotations where\nmypy's Any-widening would destroy the enforcement; this ticket imports a DICT, so it does not).\n\nMODULE-ATTRIBUTE CONSUMER STILL RESOLVES (criterion 5):\ntests/.../diffing/test_outbound_differ_session_log_exclusion.py passes UNMODIFIED — its\n`assert \"session_log\" not in _of._LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE` at :87 still resolves the name as a module\nattribute on outbound_fields. Zero test files were edited except the boundary guard.\n\nMUTATED: re-added a second dict literal {\"task\":\"Task\",\"story\":\"Story\",\"bug\":\"Bug\",\"epic\":\"Epic\"}\nunder adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py, per the plan's concrete procedure;\nFAILED: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py::test_exactly_one_type_map_literal_within_adapters\nRED counts: 1 failed, 23 passed. GREEN after revert: 24 passed. It failed for the RIGHT reason —\nthe guard's OWN assertion message, not an AttributeError/ImportError:\n  AssertionError: expected exactly one local->Jira type map literal, found:\n    ['jira_datacenter/backend.py', 'jira_family/value_maps.py']\n  assert 2 == 1\nNote the message names the offending file, so a future contributor who reintroduces a copy is\ntold where it is rather than merely that something is wrong.\n\nTESTS ADDED (all in the boundary-guard file, which is the ticket's owned test surface):\n * test_exactly_one_type_map_literal_within_adapters — the guard, same AST shape as the\n   status/priority ones (criterion 6).\n * test_both_create_paths_resolve_to_the_single_type_definition — IDENTITY (is), not equality:\n   equal copies would not prove de-duplication. Asserts outbound_fields._LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE is\n   LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA and backend._LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE is LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA.\n * test_create_paths_pin_the_issue_type_by_value — parametrized over all four local types,\n   asserting the built \"issuetype\" field through the Cloud create path\n   (_map_local_to_jira_fields) AND the DC create path (_map_local_to_dc_fields). BY VALUE, not on\n   the map's shape (criteria 7+8). These are the pins sibling cedc should reuse rather than\n   re-author.\n * the by-path spec_from_file_location load test gained a type-map assertion, since that map is\n   now an import subject to the same absolute-import requirement.\n\nGATES: make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS (mypy, 414 files). tests/unit/rebar_reconciler:\n1891 passed. Module sizes, all far under the 800 cap:\n  value_maps.py 72 -> 89; jira_family/__init__.py 65 -> 67;\n  jira/outbound_fields.py 619 -> 615 (shrank); jira_datacenter/backend.py 350 -> 357;\n  test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py 404 -> 448."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785713226620696001,"uuid":"e0229a20-cc1f-45c8-8ec8-af78d796f7fc"}